# Architecture

## Feature structure

All feature code lives in `src/features/<name>/`:

```
src/features/<name>/
  api/        API call functions (use apiClient)
  components/ React components for this feature
  hooks/      Custom hooks (useQuery, useMutation wrappers)
  types.ts    TypeScript interfaces for this feature
```

## Pages are thin

`src/pages/<Name>Page.tsx` imports from features and returns them.
No business logic, no API calls, no state in pages.

## API

- All HTTP calls go through `src/api/client.ts` (axios instance).
- The client auto-unwraps `{ data: ... }` envelopes via interceptors.
- Each feature's `api/` folder exports typed async functions.

## Auth

- Auth state in `useAuthStore` (Zustand, persisted to localStorage).
- Never store tokens in component state or context.
- Home (`/`) is public. Use `<ProtectedRoute />` for routes that require sign-in.
- Logout: call `clearAuth()`, then `navigate('/', { replace: true })`.

## Styling

- Read `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc` — must match `.arlox/design-system.json`.

## Router

- Routes defined in `src/app/router.tsx`.
- Nav links added in `src/layouts/AdminSidebar.tsx`.
